{"file":"llm-wiki-plugin-3.1.1-v2.zip","bytes":3503039,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"llm-wiki","description":"Build and maintain an LLM-curated personal knowledge base with default local FastEmbed + sqlite-vec search, BM25 fusion, structured evidence, incremental caching, and a compiled graph layer.","version":"3.1.1","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/praneybehl/llm-wiki-plugin","homepage":"https://github.com/praneybehl/llm-wiki-plugin","keywords":["knowledge-base","wiki","notes","research","second-brain","obsidian","markdown","rag-alternative","llm-wiki"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/llm-wiki/SKILL.md","name":"llm-wiki","description":"Build and maintain an LLM-curated personal knowledge base — the \"LLM Wiki\" pattern from Andrej Karpathy's April 2026 gist. Use this skill whenever the user wants to ingest a source (paper, article, transcript, PDF, notes) into a persistent compounding knowledge base, ask a question against accumulated notes, lint or audit such a base, or initialize a new one. Trigger on phrases like \"add this to my wiki\", \"ingest this paper\", \"compile this into the knowledge base\", \"what does my wiki say about X\", \"lint the wiki\", \"build a knowledge base from these documents\", \"research notes\", \"second brain\", \"personal knowledge base\", or any reference to LLM Wiki / OmegaWiki. Trigger even when the user does not say \"wiki\" — if they are accumulating sources over time and want them organized, this applies. The skill scales — sharded indexes, atomic pages, YAML frontmatter, and a bundled search script keep the wiki from becoming a context bottleneck at hundreds or thousands of pages.","headings":["LLM Wiki","The pattern in one paragraph","When to use this skill","Architecture: three layers, three operations","Graph layer (compiled, optional)","Storage scope and layout","The scalability discipline","Initializing a new wiki","Project wiki: <project-root>/wiki and <project-root>/raw","Personal global wiki: ~/wiki with raw sources at ~/wiki/raw","The ingest workflow (summary)","The query workflow (summary)","The lint workflow (summary)","Failure modes to guard against","Reference files","Bundled scripts","Templates"],"name_hint":"llm · 知识库","description_zh":"建立维护LLM整理的个人知识库，将论文、文章、转录、PDF和笔记持续纳入，支持基于累计笔记问答、检查审计和初始化；以分片索引、原子页面、YAML元数据及搜索脚本支持较大规模。"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/wiki/graph.md","name":"graph","description":"Compile, lint, or query the wiki's typed graph layer.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/wiki/ingest.md","name":"ingest","description":"Ingest a source (paper, article, transcript, PDF, notes) into the LLM Wiki.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/wiki/init.md","name":"init","description":"Initialize a personal global LLM Wiki or one in this project.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/wiki/lint.md","name":"lint","description":"Run a structural and semantic health check on the LLM Wiki.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/wiki/query.md","name":"query","description":"Query the LLM Wiki — answer a question from accumulated knowledge with citations.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/wiki/stats.md","name":"stats","description":"Show wiki size, shape, and link density — and which scaling threshold the wiki is at.","headings":[]},{"path":"commands/wiki/upgrade.md","name":"upgrade","description":"Upgrade an existing global or project LLM Wiki to the current plugin version.","headings":[]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["LLM Wiki — a second brain for AI agents","What is LLM Wiki?","What's new in v3.0.0","Why use it?","Installation","Claude Code — full plugin","Other coding agents — skill only","Install globally so the skill is available across all projects","Or install into the current project only","Choose where the wiki lives","Quick start","Commands","Architecture","How it scales","What it doesn't try to be","Integrations","Paperclip — `paperclip-plugin-llm-wiki`"]},{"path":"integrations/paperclip/README.md","headings":["Us